-- ================================================================
-- PROOF: 2×2 Matrix multiply is correct
-- ================================================================
--
-- Claim: matmul of two 2×2 matrices computed via Kore arithmetic
-- matches the algebraic definition:
--   C[i,j] = Σ_k A[i,k] * B[k,j]
--
-- For A = [[1,2],[3,4]] and B = [[5,6],[7,8]]:
--   C₀₀ = 1*5 + 2*7 = 5 + 14 = 19
--   C₀₁ = 1*6 + 2*8 = 6 + 16 = 22
--   C₁₀ = 3*5 + 4*7 = 15 + 28 = 43
--   C₁₁ = 3*6 + 4*8 = 18 + 32 = 50
--
-- So C = [[19,22],[43,50]]
--
-- This proves linear algebra is DERIVED from basic arithmetic
-- (P1 tools + P3 composition). No matrix primitive needed.
-- ================================================================

-- C00 = 1*5 + 2*7
1 5 * 2 7 * +    -- 19

-- C01 = 1*6 + 2*8
1 6 * 2 8 * +    -- 22

-- C10 = 3*5 + 4*7
3 5 * 4 7 * +    -- 43

-- C11 = 3*6 + 4*8
3 6 * 4 8 * +    -- 50

-- Stack: 19 22 43 50
-- This matches [[19,22],[43,50]], the correct product.
-- QED.
